{
  "contract": "routes.v1",
  "domain": "meetings",
  "owner": "core/meetings",
  "edge": "gateway",
  "note": "Bots, bot accounts (saved signed-in browser profiles and the sign-in sessions that make them, ADR-0049), meeting records, transcripts, recordings — and the two calendar SYNC verbs, which run against the feed meeting-api owns even though the connection itself is identity's. A row with `mcp_reentry` is one the MCP's own meeting tools call back into (core/gateway/services/mcp/src/vexa_mcp/app.py): a worker's token is admitted there on the MCP's re-entry, and on no other row. A row with `upstream` is forwarded to that path on meeting-api rather than its own; meeting-api reads this file to check, for each of its routes, the scopes of the rows that reach it (meeting_api/route_scopes.py). `GET /voice-notes/{native_meeting_id}/stream` is a WebSocket: the row is its upgrade request, and the edge relays the socket to the same path on meeting-api. The sign-in session's live-view websocket (`/bot-accounts/sessions/{session_id}/vnc`) is not a row, because routes.v1 declares HTTP verbs: the edge relays it to the same path on meeting-api and holds it to the scopes of `GET /bot-accounts/sessions/{session_id}`.",
  "presence_env": "MEETING_API_URL",
